# GitButler Update Branches

After you **generate code** or **modify files**, run the GitButler update branches MCP tool so branch state stays in sync with the changes.

## When to run

- You created, edited, or deleted source/config/docs files.
- You finished a set of related edits (e.g. feature, fix, refactor).

## How to run

Call the **`gitbutler_update_branches`** MCP tool (server: `user-gitbutler`) with:

| Parameter | Value |
|-----------|--------|
| `fullPrompt` | The exact user prompt that led to these changes |
| `changesSummary` | Short bullet list of what was changed and why |
| `currentWorkingDirectory` | Full path to the Git project root (e.g. workspace path) |

Run it once per logical change set, after your edits are done.
